   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public housing law, in relation to directing the\ncommissioner of housing and community renewal to promulgate rules and\nregulations regarding the use of electronic records and signatures for certain\nresidential leases",
    "basePrintNo": "S4742",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4742-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §19-a, Pub Hous L",
    "lawSection": "Public Housing Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S4742\n\nSPONSOR: KAMINSKY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public housing law, in relation to directing the\ncommissioner of housing and community renewal to promulgate rules and\nregulations regarding the use of electronic records and signatures for\ncertain residential leases\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe bill requires the Division of Housing and Community Renewal to\ndevelop regulations to allow electronic leases and signatures to be used\nfor leases of rent stabilized units, while also ensuring that the use of\nelectronic records is entirely voluntary for the tenant.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one requires the commissioner of the Division of Housing and\nCommunity Renewal to promulgate rules that allow for the use of elec-\ntronic records and signatures for leases and lease renewals of rent\nstabilized units on a voluntary basis by the tenant. It also requires\nthe commissioner to develop a form that confirms the voluntary use of\nelectronic records by the tenant. The form must be signed by both the\ntenant and landlord and be on file with the division before any elec-\ntronic records can be accepted.\n\nSection two sets forth the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe ability to use an electronic lease document, or to electronically\nsign a lease agreement, could prove to be more efficient than paper\nrecords for both landlords and tenants where both parties have clearly\nagreed to the use of electronic records. This bill would establish a\ndefined process for the Division of Housing and Community Renewal to\nallow the use of electronic documents and signatures for rent regulated\nleases and lease renewals, including safeguards to ensure all tenants\ncontinue to have full access to their choice of a paper or electronic\nlease record.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2020: S8864 died in rules.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nUndetermined\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThe bill shall take effect immediately.\n",
